WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.290
Compression can shorten and bend layered rocks into folds while the

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:08.190
layers remain traceable. The curved region of maximum bending is the

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.670
hinge, and the sides are limbs.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.970
Trace the same layer through the whole structure before naming a

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:13.230
fold.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.550
An anticline has older rocks in its core and a syncline

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.050
has younger rocks in its core.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:23.730
In an upright fold, anticlines commonly arch upward and synclines trough

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:28.650
downward. Overturning complicates simple shape rules, so use age relations where

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.190
they are known.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:33.470
A dome is a roughly circular structure with older rocks in

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.250
its center; a basin has younger rocks in its center.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:40.730
A monocline is a step-like bend connecting more gently dipping segments.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:44.710
Modern topography can differ because rocks erode at different rates.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.770
An axial surface joins hinges through successive layers.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.870
It can be upright or inclined.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.450
A fold is overturned where a limb has rotated beyond vertical.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:57.510
A plunging hinge is inclined rather than horizontal.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.390
These descriptions address different aspects of geometry.
